# The user the AURCache server runs as.
#
# Declared rather than created by a script: systemd-sysusers is idempotent by
# construction and re-applied on boot, where an install script has to be
# written carefully not to clobber an existing account.
#
# The worker package declares this same user in its own file. Two sysusers
# files may declare one user -- the second is a no-op -- and they must be two
# files, because pacman refuses to install two packages that ship the same
# path even when the contents are identical.
u aurcache - "AURCache server and build worker" /var/lib/aurcache -
